+/*
+ * Sublet lifetimes.  Every block a manager gets from malloc has a generation,
+ * a lifetime derived from the block's malloc reference, and every chunk is a
+ * child of the generation that covers the chunk's payload and nothing else.
+ * Freeing the block ends all of them.  A reset that keeps the block revokes
+ * the generation (CREVOKE), which ends the chunks, and the next allocation
+ * derives a new one.
